From 14782514fc03fb6d6f1253e9f021346f469c0342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 03:36:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] plugin:CPER:Processed Add extension support

Add support for the
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER Processed
extension.

Introduce a schema-backed descriptor and runtime plugin
implementation for CPER Processed metadata. The descriptor
mirrors the properties defined by the CPER Processed D-Bus
interface and is used to translate request metadata into
runtime plugin instances.

The plugin augments log entries with the
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed D-Bus
interface and exposes processed CPER metadata through
D-Bus properties, including the diagnostic data type,
notification type, section type, and OEM metadata.

Add a corresponding plugin factory and register it with
the plugin registry, enabling request-to-descriptor
translation and runtime creation of CPERProcessed plugins
through the existing plugin manager framework.

Also add build integration and unit tests covering
plugin registration, descriptor creation, request
metadata propagation, factory creation, plugin manager
integration, and descriptor property propagation.

The plugin is limited to exposing processed CPER metadata
associated with a log entry. Management of the underlying
CPER artifact and support for additional CPER-specific
extensions remain outside the scope of this change.

Tested:

'''
Generated a CPER event with extension metadata

Example:

auto cperEvent =
    sdbusplus::error::xyz::openbmc_project::state::Cper::Error(
        nlohmann::json{
            {"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Cper.Error",
             {
                 {"SOURCE",
                  "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system"},
             }},
        },
        std::source_location::current());

cperEvent.extend(
    sdbusplus::common::xyz::openbmc_project::
        logging::extension::CPER::Processed::properties_t{
            .diagnostic_data_type =
                sdbusplus::common::xyz::openbmc_project::Logging::
                    cper::Types::ContentType::CPER,
            .notification_type =
                "8f87f311-c998-4d9e-a0c4-fb4dfc2c8c14",
            .section_type =
                "dc3ea0b0-a144-4797-b95b-53fa242b6e1d",
            .oem =
                {{"Source",
                  "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system"}},
        });

lg2::commit(std::move(cperEvent));

Result:

busctl introspect xyz.openbmc_project.Logging \
  /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/1

...
...

xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed interface -         -
.DiagnosticDataType    property  s
    "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER"

.NotificationType      property  s
    "8f87f311-c998-4d9e-a0c4-fb4dfc2c8c14"

.Oem                   property  a{ss}
    "Source" : "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system"

.SectionType           property  s
    "dc3ea0b0-a144-4797-b95b-53fa242b6e1d"

xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Entry interface -         -
.AdditionalData        property  a{ss}
    5 entries

.Id                    property  u
    1

...

busctl --json=pretty call xyz.openbmc_project.Logging \
  /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/1 \
  org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties GetAll \
  s xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed

{
    "DiagnosticDataType": {
        "data": "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER"
    },
    "NotificationType": {
        "data": "8f87f311-c998-4d9e-a0c4-fb4dfc2c8c14"
    },
    "SectionType": {
        "data": "dc3ea0b0-a144-4797-b95b-53fa242b6e1d"
    },
    "Oem": {
        "data": {
            "Source": "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system"
        }
    }
}
'''

